    {
      "slug": "gram:gp-98",
      "nuance_tags": [],
      "usage_contexts": ["spoken", "written"],
      "steps_unavailable": "The pattern in the record is 何 + COUNTER + か: the interrogative 何 must PRECEDE the counter. The op enum is suffix-only (no prepend), and the base enum has no counter / interrogative-quantifier member. Base noun + append か would either yield 人か (no 何) or, applied to a plain noun, license 学生か, which is the sentence-final question particle the record explicitly warns against confusing with this か.",
      "variants": []
    },
    {
      "slug": "gram:gp-99",
      "nuance_tags": ["emphasis"],
      "usage_contexts": ["spoken", "written"],
      "steps_unavailable": "真 is a PREFIX (真っ赤, 真ん中, 真夜中); the op enum is suffix-only, so the attachment cannot be expressed. The record also states the shape is decided case by case (ま / まっ / まん) and is to be memorised as vocabulary, so no rule selects the allomorph from the following word.",
      "variants": []
    },
